      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Binford%2C_North_Dakota",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The town, originally called Blooming Prairie, was renamed Binford after attorney Ray Binford of Charles City, Iowa, who handled the Land Company's purchase.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        2
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Binford%2C_North_Dakota",
      "category": "etymology",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "By fall 1899 a lumberyard and general store opened, followed by a hotel in 1900, establishing Binford’s early commercial core.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        6,
        7
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Binford%2C_North_Dakota",
      "category": "economy",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Every June, Binford hosts Binford Days, a festival featuring a 5K run, parade, classic car show, silent auction, and a late‑night street dance.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        8,
        9
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
